# The port's half of the pi- like-for-like; its partner is pion_minus_emonly.mac. The two files
# differ only by the inactivations, which is the whole point of keeping them as a pair.
#
# MEASURED, 500,000 events. CLOSED - docs/RISK.md V46.
#
#                    port BEFORE         port AFTER          Geant4 EM-only      after
#   pi-   630.922 +/- 0.666   600.871 +/- 0.636   600.831 +/- 0.636   +0.007%, 0.04 sigma
#   pi+   632.349 +/- 0.668   632.349 +/- 0.668   633.446 +/- 0.668   -0.17%,  1.16 sigma
#
# "BEFORE" was +5.01% at 32.7 sigma. The pi+ column is BIT-IDENTICAL across the fix, which is
# what says the change selected the negative and did not simply rescale both.
#
# THE PAIR IS THE MEASUREMENT, not either number, and the pair is now right too: the port
# separates its two pions by 5.24% where Geant4 separates its own by 5.43%, against 0.226%
# before. The restricted dE/dx table this install dumps still separates them by 0.023% in
# water and 0.233% in the scored bone - Geant4's transport still does not agree with Geant4's
# own dE/dx table, and it never did. What changed is that the port stopped agreeing with the
# table and started agreeing with the transport, because the table the transport actually
# reads is the RANGE table, whose interpolation Geant4 makes linear for the second-registered
# particle of every charge pair. docs/RISK.md V46 has the five source lines; ref/chargeodd/
# has the diagnostic that found them.
#
# The rms moved with the mean: 0.666 -> 0.636 nGy, against Geant4's 0.636. A per-event spread
# that lands on the reference's is a second and independent sign that the distribution moved
# and not just its first moment.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/gun/particle pi-
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
